{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The options are similar. However, the case for $-4\\le x\u003c0$ is different.\n\nWe can see that by noting that the first case in graph $A$ ends at $(0,6)$ and the first case in graph $B$ ends at $(0,4)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The rule for the first case is $y=3x+4$. When $x=0$, the $y$-value should be $4$.\n\n**The correct graph is $B$.**\n\n[[☃ image 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"image 1":{"alignment":"block","graded":true,"options":{"alt":"correct answer","backgroundImage":{"height":225,"url":"web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/0b882b22db28c429e59f5ae2a786048f6460b73b","width":225},"box":[225,225],"caption":"","labels":[],"range":[[0,10],[0,10]],"static":false,"title":""},"static":false,"type":"image","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$g(x) = \\begin{cases}\n3x+4 \u0026 , \u0026  -4\\le x\u003c0\n\\\\\\\\\n-4 \u0026 , \u0026 0\\le x\\le 6\n\\end{cases}$\n\n**What is the graph of $g$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"![answer A](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/29e8686758b8b2c6ed8405cc63dc32644d4122cb)","correct":false},{"content":"![answer B](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/0b882b22db28c429e59f5ae2a786048f6460b73b)","correct":true}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
